    {
      "number": 1041,
      "title": "task actions: recommend only actions the lifecycle can execute",
      "body": "## Usage\n\n```bash\nlf task status W2-285 --json | jq .actions\nlf task resume W2-285   # refuses without reserving a process generation\nlf status               # settled Tasks name their real next move\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nBoth snapshot builders fed `derive_task_actions` only the *active* PR (`Working | Publishing | Open`), so `Merged` and `Abandoned` were erased before the action model ever saw them. Settled Tasks fell through the `None` arm into the body model and got recommended `Resume` — a command the runner refuses, because resume requires an active PR. The model's settled arms were reachable only from hand-built tests.\n\nAction evidence now comes from the newest PR in sequence order, while `active_pr` stays the separate operational identity used by PR commands, fresh CI, and stack-predecessor checks. A merged Task carries the completion gate's own refusal string as its reason, so status and `lf task complete` say the same thing; an abandoned latest PR recommends `start_next_pr`; and a shared `no_active_pr_resume_refusal` is evaluated by both status and `resume_task_async` before any generation is reserved. No new blocker enums, no parallel gate evaluator, no wire-shape change — the six action names and DTO shape are untouched; only recommendations and reason strings move for settled evidence.\n\nOne behavior change beyond the projection: a pending directive now independently authorizes a serial successor off a settled completing PR, alongside the existing committed-follow-up case. The successor exists precisely to incorporate the accepted direction, and completion is already gated on it.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `TaskActionEvidence` renames `active_pr_*` to `latest_pr_*` and gains `completion_refusal`, `resume_refusal`, and `pending_directive`\n- `CompletionGate::refusal()` and `no_active_pr_resume_refusal()` become the shared authorities behind both status and the mutating commands\n- `ensure_working_pr_with_authority` lets a pending directive rotate a completing PR\n- Store-backed tests prove a merged W2-285-shaped Task routes Review, blocks Complete with the exact `task_complete` error, blocks Resume with the exact `task_resume` error, and leaves `latest_process` byte-for-byte unchanged on refusal\n- `StoreEnvGuard` for tests that only read persisted state, kept distinct from `TaskLaunchEnv` (whose fake tmux on `PATH` reads as a live body to concurrent liveness tests)\n- Three pre-existing liveness tests now take the journal env lock; they raced `TaskLaunchEnv` on clean main (1 in 4 runs) and this branch's tests made it reproduce more often. Test setup only — see `scratch/questions.md`.",
      "files": [],
      "additions": 564,
      "deletions": 77,
      "changed_files": 3
    },
    {
      "number": 1042,
      "title": "ci: count autonomy only when a ci-fix command owns the repair",
      "body": "",
      "files": [],
